# Frequently Asked Questions

Short answers. Follow the linked page when you need the contract.

## What is Rocci?

Rocci lets you write HTML in Roc, run a small app from `.rocci` files, and
optionally publish Markdown on that same stack. Start with
[the stack](/docs/the-stack/).

## Is Rocci a client-side JavaScript framework?

No. Rocci renders HTML from Roc. Datastar is the browser transport for
requests, patches, commands, and streams. Durable state stays on the
server. Read [Handlers](/docs/applications/handlers/).

## When should I use `.rocci` or `.rocdown`?

Use `.rocci` when view structure and Roc logic lead. Use `.rocdown` when
prose leads, then `.rocci` for the site shell. See
[Rocdown pages](/docs/rocdown/pages/).

## Can Rocdown publish interactive pages?

Yes, as an experimental extra. A hybrid site publishes CDN HTML and runs
a sibling island service for pages with handlers. The reserved `@island`
syntax is not implemented. See
[Publish a hybrid site](/docs/rocdown/hybrid/).

## Can I build desktop applications?

`rocci run` can open a preview window, and `rocci bundle` can create a
local, ad-hoc-signed macOS `.app`. Production signing, installers, and
updates are not shipped. See
[Compatibility](/docs/reference/compatibility/).

## Is Rocci ready for production adoption?

Treat it as an active experiment. Current limits are on
[Project status](/project/status/).

## How do I send feedback?

Use GitHub issues:
[github.com/koliyo/rocci/issues](https://github.com/koliyo/rocci/issues).
Pick the **bug** or **docs** form. Do not open a pull request expecting a
merge. Security reports go to
[SECURITY.md](https://github.com/koliyo/rocci/blob/main/SECURITY.md).
